# Part of the "venus3d" module -- see venus3dService.js's installVtestSocketProp() for the
# full story. minigbm's own patched NVIDIA backend (external/minigbm/nvidia_venus.c in this
# project's AOSP tree, nvidia_venus_connect()) does not read the VTEST_SOCKET_NAME environment
# variable Mesa's Vulkan ICD uses (vn_renderer_create_vtest(), set via surfaceflinger.rc's own
# setenv) -- it reads this system property instead, via __system_property_get(), falling back to
# a hardcoded /dev/venus/venus.sock (not this module's actual socket path) if unset. Without this,
# any gralloc.cros.so consumer -- most importantly the legacy HIDL 2.0 Allocator service
# SurfaceFlinger's own GraphicBufferAllocator depends on for real display buffers -- fails with
# ENODEV ("no vtest connection") and crash-loops.
#
# An EIGHTH real gap, found after SurfaceFlinger's own RenderEngine booted correctly but every
# app's EGL path (HWUI/ANGLE, used by SystemUI, launcher3, and any scrcpy-driven virtual
# display) still crash-looped with "ANGLE Display::initialize error 0: Internal Vulkan error
# (-3)": zygote-forked app processes never see the `setenv VTEST_SOCKET_NAME/VN_DEBUG` pair
# patchSurfaceflingerRc()/patchLegacyGrallocRc() set -- those are scoped to one service's own
# forked process, and zygote does not inherit init's environment the way a directly-forked
# service does. But Mesa's os_get_option() (src/util/os_misc.c, os_get_android_option()) already
# falls back from getenv() to a system property for every env var it reads on Android, readable
# by any process regardless of how it was forked: VTEST_SOCKET_NAME -> mesa.vtest.socket.name
# (already set below), VN_DEBUG -> mesa.vn.debug. And VN_DEBUG=vtest is not cosmetic --
# vn_renderer_create() (src/virtio/vulkan/vn_renderer.h) only attempts the vtest transport at all
# when VN_DEBUG(VTEST) is set; without it, it falls through to vn_renderer_create_vtgpu(), which
# tries a real virtio-gpu kernel device that does not exist here, producing the exact generic
# VK_ERROR_INITIALIZATION_FAILED (err=-3) ANGLE was logging. Setting mesa.vn.debug here makes
# every process -- zygote-forked apps included -- resolve the same vtest path SurfaceFlinger's
# own setenv already gave it, with no per-service wiring needed.
on early-init
    setprop mesa.vtest.socket.name /vendor/venus.sock
    setprop mesa.vn.debug vtest
